# --- StudPlacer (Inventor iLogic tool) ---------------------------------------
# The blanket *.csv above exists to keep the multi-hundred-MB model extracts out
# of the repo. StudPlacer's rule tables are the opposite kind of file: small,
# hand-maintained SOURCE transcribed from drawing 008N9536, and the iLogic
# engine refuses to start without them. Likewise 'parts/' is ignored above as a
# Python packaging convention, but here it holds the stud .ipt library.
#
# These were silently excluded once already, which is why the tool ran fine
# locally and failed on a fresh clone with "code tables not found".
# tools/check_deployable.py now fails the test run if that recurs.
!Inventor/StudPlacer/rules/
!Inventor/StudPlacer/rules/*.csv
!Inventor/StudPlacer/samples/
!Inventor/StudPlacer/samples/*.csv
!Inventor/StudPlacer/parts/
